  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sardar S/O Omkar vs State Of Rajasthan (2024:Rj-Jp:12670) on 13 March, 2024 Author: Praveer Bhatnagar Bench: Praveer Bhatnagar [2024:RJ-JP:12670] HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE FOR RAJASTHAN BENCH AT JAIPUR S.B. Criminal Miscellaneous Bail Application No. 3080/2024 1. Sardar S/o Omkar, Aged About 40 Years, R/o Mahasingh Ka Bas, Police Station Viratnagar, District Kotputli Behror. (At Present Confined In Central Jail, Kotputli). 2. Digamber S/o Harisingh, Aged About 29 Years, R/o Sancholi, Police Station Kaushi, District Mathura, Uttar Pradesh. (At Present Confined In Central Jail, Kotputli). 3. Surajpal S/o Premsingh, Aged About 39 Years, R/o Basfateli, Police Station Eglas, District Aligarh, U.p. (At Present Confined In Central Jail, Kotputli). ----Petitioners Versus State Of Rajasthan, Through Pp, Shahpura, District Jaipur, Rajasthan. ----Respondent For Petitioner(s) : Mr. Gaurav Singh Tanwar For Respondent(s) : Mr. C. G. Chopra-PP HON'BLE MR. JUSTICE PRAVEER BHATNAGAR Order 13/03/2024 The instant bail application has been filed under Section 439 Cr.P.C. on behalf of accused-petitioners.",
    "facts": "The petitioners have been arrested in connection with FIR No.89/2024 registered at Police Station Shahpura (Jaipur Rural), District Jaipur Rural for the offence(s) under Sections 420, 270, 272, 273 and 120B of IPC.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners submits that the accused- petitioners have been falsely implicated in the case. He further contends that police has no right to initiate the proceedings under Sections 270, 272 and 273 of IPC as under Section 89 of the Food [2024:RJ-JP:12670] (2 of 2) [CRLMB-3080/2024] Safety Act, only concerned Food Inspector can initiate the proceedings. Per contra, learned Public Prosecutor vehemently opposes the bail application."
  },
